Minister your vision of ASEAN for the future. 

00:19:44.550 --> 00:19:49.621
Well I think we hope that ASEAN remains

00:19:49.988 --> 00:19:58.130
safe prosperous and pleased. And for each week we can each

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:03.869
improve the well-being of people living in ASEAN. All this work

00:20:03.902 --> 00:20:07.472
that we are doing on economy integration financial integration

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:13.679
on promoting fintech and so on ultimately has one simple aim

00:20:13.679 --> 00:20:17.216
which is to improve the wellbeing of our people in ASEAN. And

00:20:17.216 --> 00:20:21.920
with that I think we can maintain peace and

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:27.159
stability in ASEAN. We contribute to the global peace and prosperity.

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:29.795
I think we need respect that we are seeing in the

00:20:29.928 --> 00:20:36.001
Western countries. We receive more ASEAN with greater wealth

00:20:36.001 --> 00:20:42.474
generated so there will be more demand and diversity greater

00:20:42.474 --> 00:20:47.980
segmentation and certain areas like the wealth management 

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:51.350
poverty will increasingly be significant and important. 

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:55.854
I think ASEAN should realise within itself what are the strengths and what are

00:20:55.921 --> 00:20:59.324
the weaknesses. Some countries obviously have very strong

00:20:59.324 --> 00:21:03.328
ability to do certain things and other countries have a

00:21:03.328 --> 00:21:06.365
different. Singapore is never going to be an agricultural giant

00:21:06.365 --> 00:21:11.803
. It's never going to do but it has very strong financial

00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:16.942
infrastructure. So I think each country should not try and

00:21:16.942 --> 00:21:20.746
replicate everything but see where they have the niche. 

00:21:20.746 --> 00:21:26.285
We have a lot more economic activities. We have a lot more common

00:21:26.285 --> 00:21:31.490
problems that we have to deal with it and technology will

00:21:31.523 --> 00:21:35.761
basically blur the boundaries across countries.

00:21:35.761 --> 00:21:38.163
 So we have to think more in terms of creating win-win

00:21:38.196 --> 00:21:43.035
opportunities in our ASEAN integration framework to promote

00:21:43.035 --> 00:21:47.773
growth and to promote sustainable prosperity for ASEAN citizens. 

00:21:47.773 --> 00:21:52.711
I think ASEAN should be much more careful and pragmatic so there be

00:21:52.711 --> 00:21:56.748
controlled flows of labour and already if I'm not mistaken

00:21:56.848 --> 00:22:01.687
millions of Indonesians work in Malaysia, Singapore has got  

00:22:01.687 --> 00:22:04.556
1.7 million foreigners working in this small island city

00:22:04.556 --> 00:22:09.795
state of Singapore Thailand gets a lot of workers from Myanmar

00:22:09.795 --> 00:22:14.700
coming in. So there is steady movement of labour but there'll

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:18.337
never be a kind of the kind of freedom of movement that you have

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:22.708
for example with the European Union. My dream for ASEAN is

00:22:22.708 --> 00:22:28.880
that it will continue to stay together and not break apart as a

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:32.184
result of US China rivalry because there's one thing that keeps me

00:22:32.284 --> 00:22:36.788
awake at night. It's worrying about how ASEAN will survive this

00:22:36.788 --> 00:22:43.695
incredibly intense U.S. China rivalry that is coming in the next 10 to 20 years.

00:22:45.764 --> 00:22:49.735
From source the ocean the Mekong River flows for

00:22:49.735 --> 00:22:53.605
more than 4000 kilometers the main artery that for centuries

00:22:53.605 --> 00:22:58.844
connected this part of the world. But times are changing fast .

00:22:58.844 --> 00:23:02.714
Massive infrastructure projects and the digital revolution are

00:23:02.714 --> 00:23:09.287
creating a whole new future. Thanks for watching. ASEAN: The Next Generation

